  "aiContextParagraph": "The political discourse in Indonesia has increasingly focused on potential candidates for the vice presidency, with Sufmi Dasco Ahmad emerging as a prominent figure gaining support from various sectors. Endorsements have been voiced by multiple stakeholders, including the Wali Nanggroe Aceh, the Indonesian Ulema Council (MUI), and the central board of Pemuda Muhammadiyah. Supporters characterize him as a multitalented consolidator who possesses the necessary vision and political acumen to serve alongside President Prabowo. While public discussions regarding the role continue, there have been mentions of external efforts to influence the narrative surrounding his potential nomination. These endorsements have surfaced amid broader political activities, such as private meetings with labor alliances and cabinet-related discussions, drawing reactions from political observers and former government officials.",
